    "VISUAL_NAME": "Gauge",
    "SCHEMA_NAME": "FAM_DEPRECIATION_POSTING_COMPLIANCE",
    "SCHEMA_DESCR": "VIS_011 - Monthly Depreciation Posting Compliance (Gauge vs 100% target) for the Management Dashboard. SEVERE ASSUMPTION (data availability): the Generate Depreciation - Companies Act (Monthly) process is designed to persist FAM_DEP_COMPANIES_ACT_REGISTER (one row per asset per financial_year+period_month, with a STATUS reaching APPROVED on Approve & Post), but that table has never actually been generated in this environment (no Generate + Approve & Post cycle has been run) and does not exist in the live database - describe_table/run_select on it fail with 'relation does not exist'. It therefore CANNOT be queried, so COMPLIANCE_PCT cannot be computed as a true 'assets with current-period depreciation posted' count; the visual instead reports a literal 0% (the numerator is definitionally 0 while no period has ever been posted), computed against a REAL, filtered eligible-asset denominator (FAM_ASSET_REGISTER rows with STATUS='ACTIVE', CAPITALIZATION_DATE on/before the selected financial_year's FY-end, matching the selected branch_code) so the query still exercises the dashboard's financial_year/branch_code criteria and always returns exactly one row (subquery COUNT(*) never returns zero rows). TARGET/MIN/MAX are the fixed 100/0/100 gauge scale the FRS specifies ('Gauge vs 100% target'). Once the Companies Act depreciation process is actually run and FAM_DEP_COMPANIES_ACT_REGISTER is deployed and populated, COMPLIANCE_PCT should be swapped to 100.0 * (COUNT of eligible assets with a FAM_DEP_COMPANIES_ACT_REGISTER row for the selected financial_year/current PERIOD_MONTH and STATUS='APPROVED') / (COUNT of eligible assets), keeping the same financial_year/branch_code criteria. financial_year is a 'YYYY-YY' string prompt (default '2026-27', matching the dashboard's global FINANCIAL_YEAR default) parsed via split_part(?.financial_year,'-',1) to derive the FY-Mar-31 cutoff; branch_code is the standard like + '%' prompt with an F2 lookup to FAM_BRANCH_MASTER, filtering FAM_ASSET_REGISTER.BRANCH_CODE directly (kept current by the Asset Transfer approval flow).",
    "SCHEMA_TYPE": "S",
    "OUTPUT_TYPE": "JSON",
    "DATABASE_TYPE": "1",
    "DATABASE_DETAIL": { "DATABASE_NAME": "PostgreSQL", "TYPE": 1 }
  },
